  "_readme": [
    "Shared file for Dr Awing. Two things live here, both of them public information:",
    "tournament pages, and how team names differ between the public sites and ours.",
    "Nothing internal belongs in this file — no match identifiers, no host names, and",
    "no notes about why something is or is not offered.",
    "",
    "tournaments[] — where a tournament's scraper values come from",
    "  ids     the tournament numbers this event has. One real event is often several",
    "          tournaments, one per tier, and they all share the same source page.",
    "  name    the tournament name, case-insensitive. Used when no id matches.",
    "  pattern regular expression; best for status:none rules that outlive a season.",
    "  sport   cs2 | valorant | dota2 | lol",
    "  url     the page to take the scraper values from",
    "  status  'none' = no usable source; its matches stop being flagged for everyone",
    "",
    "teamAliases — what the public sites call a team -> what we call it.",
    "  Keys are lowercase. One person solves a mismatch once and nobody repeats it.",
    "  The Tournament BL Check tab produces these lines ready to paste.",
    "",
    "Files written before version 4 used a different key name for ids; the older",
    "spelling is still read, so nothing already published has to be rewritten."
  ],
